  "description": "<p>When a user deletes a resource a tomstone is put in its place.  Users have expressed a desire be able to \"undelete\"   the deleted resource.   To this end,  several things must be considered/implemented.</p>\n<ol>\n\t<li>Resources that were not created as \"versionable\" cannot be undeleted.</li>\n\t<li>When a resource is deleted,  a memento of the resource's state just before deletion should be created (otherwise there will be nothing to restore should the need arise).</li>\n\t<li>The timemap should be preserved when a resource is deleted.</li>\n\t<li>It should be possible to restore a memento  via a GET on the desired version followed by PUT on against the tombstone resource.</li>\n\t<li>We may need to employ a Prefer header such as \"Prefer: ignore-tombstone\"  in order to get bypass the tombstone's 415 response on a PUT.</li>\n</ol>\n",
